       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for adults: 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for most extended-release products. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg per day,** for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg to 1,000 mg twice daily.** This is a typical dose range.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
